meta {
  name: Create Form
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/clients/{{clientId}}/forms
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Contact form",
    "description": "Contact form on acme.com",
    "payloadSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["email", "name"],
      "properties": {
        "email": { "type": "string", "format": "email" },
        "name": { "type": "string" },
        "message": { "type": "string" }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "integrations": [
      {
        "integrationId": "aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa",
        "fieldMapping": { "email": "email" }
      },
      {
        "integrationId": "bbbbbbbb-bbbb-4bbb-8bbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb",
        "fieldMapping": {}
      }
    ],
    "channels": [
      {
        "channelId": "cccccccc-cccc-4ccc-8ccc-cccccccccccc",
        "subject": "New contact form submission",
        "includeFields": null,
        "integrationIds": [
          "aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa",
          "bbbbbbbb-bbbb-4bbb-8bbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb"
        ]
      },
      {
        "channelId": "dddddddd-dddd-4ddd-8ddd-dddddddddddd",
        "message": "New contact form submission",
        "integrationIds": ["aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa"]
      },
      {
        "channelId": "eeeeeeee-eeee-4eee-8eee-eeeeeeeeeeee",
        "subject": "Someone filled in the contact form",
        "includeFields": ["name", "email"],
        "integrationIds": []
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Creates a form and all of its links in one transaction (SOL-51). Replace
  the placeholder ids with real ones: integrations and channels must already
  exist under this client (create them first).

  The example, with placeholder ids standing in for:
    aaaa… = a Mailchimp integration     cccc… = "Sales team" email group
    bbbb… = a Google Sheets integration dddd… = "#leads" Slack channel
                                        eeee… = "Ops" email group
  The form runs Mailchimp and Sheets. Sales gets an email reporting both
  results; #leads gets a Slack message reporting only Mailchimp's; Ops gets
  a plain "form submitted" email with just name and email, reporting no
  integration results.

  How the body maps onto the tables:
    integrations[]                 → form_integrations
      integrationId (required), fieldMapping (default {}): the form's
      fields → that integration's fields
    channels[]                     → form_channels
      channelId (required); optional: template (default
      "form_submission"), subject (email only), includeFields (null =
      every submitted field), message (fixed text, e.g. Slack)
    channels[].integrationIds[]    → form_channel_integrations
      which of this form's integrations that channel's notification reports
      on: one row per (channel, integration). Each must also be in
      integrations[]; empty = reports on none.

  This example writes 1 form, 2 form_integrations, 3 form_channels, and 3
  form_channel_integrations rows: (Sales, Mailchimp), (Sales, Sheets),
  (#leads, Mailchimp).

  integrations and channels are optional (default []): create a bare form
  and add links later with Link Form Integration / Link Form Channel.

  201 responds with the same shape as Get Form. 422 VALIDATION_ERROR with
  details.integrationIds / details.channelIds naming ids that aren't this
  client's (unknown and other-client ids are treated the same), or for a
  channel reporting on an integration not in integrations[]. 404 if the
  client doesn't exist.
}
